{"output":"I’ll inspect the search code and existing tests, add a minimal stale-request guard, and run the tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nThe controller lets every request update state, even after a newer search starts. I added a request counter that also advances when the query is cleared. I’ll run the existing tests and an in-memory race-condition probe, since the tests only cover normal searches.\n\nAdded a request counter so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race-condition probe passed; git diff --check passed. Combined exit code: 0.\n\nNo tests modified, dependencies installed, or blockers.","final_output":"Added a request counter so only the latest search updates results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; node --input-type=module race-condition probe passed; git diff --check passed. Combined exit code: 0.\n\nNo tests modified, dependencies installed, or blockers.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":10,"tool_calls":[{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"pwd; git status --short; ls -a","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-m_m99ddq/3-2-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":193,"stdout_bytes":135,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-c36e3ee1cf8a82cd9af92b755a850bce.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test\nnode --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst pending = [];\nconst c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => pending.push({ resolve, reject })) });\nconst result = [{ id: 'new', title: 'New', url: '/new' }];\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  const old = c.search('old');\n  const current = c.search('new');\n  const [a, b] = pending.splice(0);\n  const loading = c.getState();\n  a[outcome](outcome === 'resolve' ? result : new Error('stale'));\n  await old;\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), loading);\n  b.resolve(result);\n  await current;\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'new', results: result, loading: false, error: null });\n}\nconst old = c.search('old');\nconst current = c.search('new');\nconst [a, b] = pending.splice(0);\nb.resolve(result);\nawait current;\na.resolve([]);\nawait old;\nassert.deepEqual(c.getState().results, result);\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  const request = c.search('pending');\n  const [p] = pending.splice(0);\n  const clearing = c.search('  ');\n  const empty = { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null };\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), empty);\n  p[outcome](outcome === 'resolve' ? result : new Error('stale'));\n  await Promise.all([request, clearing]);\n  assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), empty);\n}\nconsole.log('Race-condition probe passed');\nNODE\n git diff --check; git diff --stat; git diff -- src/search/controller.ts","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-m_m99ddq/3-2-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":366,"stdout_bytes":2231,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-f228f6932cf61a50006ea5c2d9d296b4.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null